                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A very roughly-made, short, depressing tale about a sad little girl. I like the art style and music, and the story is vaguely touching, but as a game it's pretty bad.\n\nTo begin with, the game doesn't tell you anything about its controls, which are btw [b]WASD for movement, E for interaction[/b]. I only realised this after watching someone on youtube struggle with figuring it out. The camera pans with mouse movements, so I thought this was a point-and-click game and tried clicking on and dragging everything on the screen to no avail.\n\nOnce I could interact with the game, it's basically a linear adventure game with a handful of short puzzles, some timed. The little girl's story is told in little vignettes - some are memories, some are dreamlike.\n\nThere is some sort of voice acting, but it's all distorted and repetitive, mostly sounds like gibberish, only a few lines sound English.\n\nI think I reached the end [spoiler]when some teddy bears said to each other something like \"too bad she didn't find the sweeties\"[/spoiler], then the screen went black, and I got dumped to the main menu. Maybe this was a \"bad ending\"? Not sure, but the game is rough enough that I don't want to start another playthrough to find out.",
